& [Purpose]
  + compile one exact supplied SJS scope-wide hint covenant operative frame recovery-source set and controlled-forgetting policy into a deterministic restoration-tested attention basis
  + prove only local irreducibility under the declared finite candidate generator while retaining every attempt refusal and admitted release as an auditable restoration witness

& [ProfilesAndBounds]
  + [MRF-001] request profile is cantor-sjs-minimum-recoverable-frame-request/0.1 envelope profile is cantor-sjs-minimum-recoverable-frame-envelope/0.1 verification profile is cantor-sjs-minimum-recoverable-frame-verification/0.1 and evidence profile is cantor-sjs-minimum-recoverable-frame-evidence/0.1
  + [MRF-002] strict compact UTF-8 canonical JSON denies unknown duplicate noncanonical and trailing content and is bounded to outer bytes 2097152 evidence bytes 8388608 depth 48 fields 32768 and ordinary text 4096
  + [MRF-003] jobs are 1 through 32 hints 1 through 64 recovery sources 1 through 16 source references 1 through 64 set fields 0 through 128 receipts 0 through 64 candidate group size 1 through 4 and pass budget 1 through 256 with checked arithmetic
  + [MRF-004] input class is exactly synthetic_provider_free_fixture or supplied_unobserved_declaration and the known retained fixture cannot be relabeled as supplied unobserved

& [ScopeAndFrame]
  + [MRF-005] request binds distinct nonnil lowercase UUID-bearing request scope covenant frame policy and run identities exact source snapshot parent source substrate audit input class nonauthority evidence references and self-excluding request digest
  + [MRF-006] JustificationScope binds subject purpose sorted unique job identities inclusive turn interval declared model provider and tool-policy identities authority ceiling completion conditions invalidation conditions and scope digest
  + [MRF-007] OperativeFrame binds exact scope source authority policy model provider tool job latest-receipt and checkpoint identities; sorted unique constraints denials open requirements dependencies evidence obligations unresolved frontier and stop conditions; subject purpose intended transform and frame digest
  + [MRF-008] P0 semantic-correspondence fields subject purpose and intended transform compare as exact canonical strings; no embedding model confidence synonym or unreviewed semantic equivalence is accepted
  + [MRF-009] the common covenant applies to every declared job and turn in scope; job-local stitches may add data but cannot remove common hints alter scope or widen authority
  + [MRF-010] scope source authority policy model provider tool job receipt checkpoint completion or invalidation drift invalidates the compiled basis rather than silently recompiling it

& [CovenantAndRecovery]
  + [MRF-011] hint classes are exactly mandatory_governing_anchor mandatory_denial mandatory_open_obligation stable_relation recoverable_coordinate optional_trajectory_cue and expired_item
  + [MRF-012] each hint binds unique identity class term intended transform applicability completion invalidation restoration role sorted unique source references sorted unique recovery-source identities release eligibility retention floor and self-excluding digest
  + [MRF-013] mandatory governing anchors denials and open obligations have retention floor one and release eligibility false; expired items have floor zero and all other eligibility is explicit without overriding mandatory rules
  + [MRF-014] initial basis is ordered unique contains every mandatory hint contains no completed invalidated or expired hint and references only covenant hints; every covered job receives its exact basis identity
  + [MRF-015] recovery-source kinds are exactly exact_checkpoint exact_event_ledger and exact_source_artifact; each source binds one exact candidate OperativeFrame and self-excluding digest as supplied data
  + [MRF-016] a retained hint makes only its declared recovery sources reachable; zero reachable exact frames is underdetermined, more than one distinct reachable frame is underdetermined, one frame unequal to the baseline is drifted and one byte-identical frame is anchored

& [ControlledForgetting]
  + [MRF-017] candidate strategy is exactly lexicographic_single_then_grouped: release eligible hint identities are tried singly then in lexicographic combinations through max group size, bounded by pass budget
  + [MRF-018] every candidate is a strict ordered subset, never releases a retained-floor hint, preserves all mandatory hint identities and records the exact before basis candidate basis released identities and reachable recovery sources
  + [MRF-019] an anchored candidate is admitted, emits release_admitted, becomes the next basis and restarts candidate enumeration; drifted emits release_refused_drifted and underdetermined emits release_refused_underdetermined without changing the admitted basis
  + [MRF-020] every attempt emits an immutable RestorationWitness binding ordinal basis identities released hints recovery sources reconstructed-frame digest comparison outcome disposition reason and self-excluding witness digest
  + [MRF-021] compilation emits locally_irreducible only after the complete declared generator finds no admissible smaller candidate at the latest basis; budget exhaustion emits bounded_pass_budget_exhausted and makes no minimum claim
  + [MRF-022] admitted basis count and canonical serialized bytes decrease monotonically; exact source events and recovery data remain outside the active projection and no destructive forgetting occurs
  + [MRF-023] NarrativeProjection is a deterministic public event account over witness identities outcomes dispositions and reasons and is neither hidden chain of thought nor authority nor a replacement for exact witnesses

& [VerificationAndFailure]
  + [MRF-024] request scope hint frame source policy basis witness envelope and evidence digests are domain-separated deterministic and self-excluding; caller order is normalized only where fields are declared sets
  + [MRF-025] independent verification reparses retained request bytes recompiles twice byte-compares envelope witnesses final basis narrative projection verification and reconstructed evidence manifest without trusting producer counts outcomes or digests
  + [MRF-026] verification reports exact jobs hints mandatory hints initial and final basis counts recovery sources attempts admitted releases drift refusals underdetermined refusals local-minimum state budget state narrative events evidence references and fourteen effect counters; all effects are zero
  + [MRF-027] unknown duplicate overbound profile identity source scope class floor eligibility basis recovery ambiguity stale digest raw-byte witness order outcome disposition minimum budget narrative authority and fully redigested semantic mutations fail closed with typed faults and no partial output

